  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "Prep ingredients: Preheat the oven to 200C. Line an oven tray with baking paper. Thinly slice the capsicum and onion. Crush 1 garlic clove (see Make it yours). Cut the haloumi into 1cm-thick strips. Put 2 tsp fennel seeds (see Make it yours) and 2 tsp olive oil in a large bowl. Add the capsicum, onion and haloumi and toss to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/253375/photos/large/prep_ingredients-3ae71b1c8faf278962e0b40502237c25.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Roast veggies and haloumi: Put the haloumi mixture on the lined tray and season with salt and pepper. Roast for 15-18 mins, turning halfway, until the haloumi is golden and the veggies are tender.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/253376/photos/large/roast_veggies_and_haloumi-91418f7f027e646c9d267832301dc821.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Warm tortillas: Meanwhile, enclose the tortillas in foil. Put in the oven for 8 mins or until softened and warmed through.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/253377/photos/large/warm_tortillas-bf0141146a543c9f8f267750bccb030a.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make rocket salsa: Put the rocket, 2 tsp red wine vinegar and 2 tsp olive oil in a bowl, season with salt and pepper and stir to combine. Put the yoghurt and garlic in a bowl and stir to combine.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/253378/photos/large/make_rocket_salsa-7456a01eda3a461e323421686653e820.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serve up: Spread the tortillas with the garlic yoghurt. Divide the haloumi mixture and rocket salsa among the tortillas and enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/253379/photos/large/serve_up-689824d1ba136ba648e3a07f843ba16f.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "Make it yours: If you find the flavour of raw garlic too strong, toss the garlic through the veggies and haloumi before roasting, or simply leave it out. ~ Not a fan of fennel? Toss half the haloumi and veggie mixture in the fennel seeds and leave the other half plain. Roast on a separate tray, rotating trays halfway.",
      "imageUrl": "https://marleyspoon.com/media/recipe_card_steps/253380/photos/large/make_it_yours-b70d8071e0e6ae8b4ec801ac3328ec62.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
